      "description": "What the recommendation-extraction skill read out of library entry `9789240116191-eng` (Digital transformation handbook for health product catalogue), which lives in who-iris since 2026-10-30 (who-iris#107): the L1 A-Box graph `l1.json`, the L2 scenario candidates `scenarios/scenario-candidates.l2.json`, and the curation, vocabulary and run context behind them. smart-base's own analysis (owner, 2026-10-16: \"l1-extraction is part of smart-base\"), so it stays here, at `l1-extractions/<entry>/`, and cites its source entry wherever that entry is held. Declared so it is part of the knowledge graph and published (owner, 2026-10-12, bean 8pzh item 1). It sat inside `library/<entry>/` until the entry moved; a library folder holding only the extraction then read as a second copy of the entry, and folio-assistant's library ingest refused the duplicate slug. One entry per extracted library entry, never a wildcard: `scripts/l1-extraction-declared.test.ts` fails when an `l1-extractions/<entry>/` on disk is undeclared, or a declaration names one that is not there.",
